        "date": "2026-11-20T16:11:22Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into issue/2834-display-quality-shadow-ao\n\nRefresh after #2931 (\"Wireframe, see-through\", d5621be06) merged.\n\nConflicted files:\n- crates/ui/src/draw_list.rs (plan_with): keep this PR's face pipe\n  choice (FacesDepthOnly / FacesOccluded / Faces) and wrap its push in\n  main's `!display.sees_through()` guard. `wireframe` is main's\n  `display.is_wireframe()`, so the shadow and stock checks cover the new\n  mode.\n- crates/ui/src/draw_list_tests.rs: keep both sides (the three #2834\n  pins and main's see-through pin).\n- crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs: keep both `mod display_quality;` and\n  `mod see_through;`.\n\nSemantic edits (the new mode is a wireframe mode):\n- draw_list::plan_with: see above (no face pass, no shadow, no\n  occlusion in see-through).\n- shade_cache::collect: `state.display.is_wireframe()` replaces\n  `== DisplayMode::Wireframe`, so see-through builds no shade data.\n- display_menu::quality: the two switches are disabled in both\n  wireframe modes; the tooltip says \"The wireframe modes\".\n\nTests: draw_list pins and\ndisplay_quality::wireframe_disables_the_two_switches_and_keeps_their_values\nnow also check see-through; new\nshade_cache::tests::the_wireframe_modes_build_no_shade_data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
