    "sha": "f8d4e8a4aca524d37ff93b03df356f81ad323d91",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGY4ZDRlOGE0YWNhNTI0ZDM3ZmY5M2IwM2RmMzU2ZjgxYWQzMjNkOTE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T18:39:52Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T18:39:52Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into issue/2834-display-quality-shadow-ao\n\nSecond refresh, after #2989 (wide anti-aliased overlay lines and MSAA,\n3c761b5bb) merged.\n\nConflicted files:\n- crates/app/src/view.rs: ViewPrefs keeps both field sets (ground_shadow,\n  ambient_occlusion; line_width, antialias), each with its serde default,\n  and Default sets all four. A view file of either PR alone still loads.\n- crates/ui/src/state_view.rs: load_view_from and persist_view carry all\n  four fields; State::effects and select_line_width / select_antialias\n  are all kept.\n- crates/ui/src/egui_app/display_menu.rs: both constant sets and imports.\n  Both sides named a function `quality`: #2958's is now `lines`. Order in\n  Graphics: projection, \"Line width\", \"Anti-aliasing\", separator, then the\n  #2834 presets and switches.\n- crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/display_quality.rs (add/add): one module\n  with the 8 tests of #2834 and the 5 tests of #2958. #2958's helper\n  `open_menu(file, offered)` is now `open_menu_kept`; its `disabled` fn\n  replaces the local closure of the #2834 test. The duplicate\n  `mod display_quality;` line in egui_app/tests.rs is removed.\n- crates/ui/src/viewport.rs:\n  - fields: `shade` and `_msaa_tex` / `msaa_view` kept.\n  - shader: SHADER + wide::WIDE_SHADER + shade_pass::WGSL (no name clash).\n  - constructor: #2958's pipes::make_targets(.., 1); ShadePass::new gets\n    the sample count (1, the pass's first count).\n  - #2958's segment `set_overlay` and accessors kept; #2834's `set_shade`\n    and `set_effects` kept; the old vertex `set_overlay` dropped.\n  - render match: every arm of both, in #2958's `self.pipes.*` naming.\n  - set_samples also calls `self.shade.rebuild(..)`.\n\nSample count of each shade pipeline (crates/ui/src/shade_pass.rs):\n- occluded faces (`viewport3d-occluded`): the pass's count. It draws in\n  the one 3D pass into its colour (MSAA) and depth targets.\n- ground shadow (`viewport3d-ground-shadow`): the pass's count, for the\n  same reason. Neither pipeline has a target of its own, so no shade\n  pipeline stays at 1 sample.\nShadePass stores `samples`, builds both through one `pipelines(..)` fn,\nand has `rebuild(..)` and `samples()`. View3D has `shade_samples()`.\n\nTests:\n- New gpu_render::shade_msaa::\n  set_samples_rebuilds_the_shade_pipelines_for_one_and_four_samples\n  (4x then 1x, both shade passes on: the counts agree, a frame renders\n  with no validation panic, and the passes draw).\n- layout_window_display_menu lists \"Line width\" and \"Anti-aliasing\".\n- The see-through edits of the first refresh stand: draw_list::plan_with,\n  shade_cache::collect and display_menu::quality read is_wireframe().\n- Decision record: section \"Merge with #2958\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
